"""PRE-REGISTERED momentum-space test of Luscher's locality condition for the U(1)_Y anomaly of the overlap at
Wilson mass m0 = 1.0, with a control at m0 = 0.6 (criteria fixed before any computation: criteria_pre_run.txt).
Machinery copied from luscher-L8 (only M0 changes): Wilson kernel r = 1, H = g5 (D_W - m0), q_Y(x) = tr sign H_Y(x,x)
for one Weyl component of hypercharge Y; A = sum_species m Y q_Y; contents: the 16 per family, and a lone L doublet.
Axis-restricted U(1) backgrounds U2 = exp(i th2(x1)), U4 = exp(i th4(x3)); H is exactly block diagonal in (p2, p4),
sign H exact per block (dense eigh). Lattices L x T x L x T (T = 24, or 16 for L = 24, along x2, x4).
Luscher (1998/99, supplied): q_Y = 2 Y^2 T + d*k_Y, k_Y local; the 16 has sum m Y^3 = 0, the doublet does not.
This runner re-verifies small cases live (< 100 s) and evaluates the pre-set criteria on the Mac-mini results stored
in the EMBEDDED JSON string below (no data files are read). Pre-set verdicts (MET / NOT MET) are recorded in
EXPECTED; each criterion line certifies that its verdict reproduces. H1-H3 are labelled post-hoc analyses. Finite-lattice U(1) diagnostic only; numpy only; seeded."""
